    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.18) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.01) headlining our offensive attack. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** draws a favorable matchup against Dobnak (xERA 4.62), and while the platoon splits are slightly suboptimal, his base power projection and the bump from the #3 hole keep his floor remarkably high. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a massive 14% boost due to dynamic platoon advantages against King, making him an essential start. **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) and **Miguel Vargas** (62.46) also emerge as core plays; both capitalize on a high-upside matchup against Ober, where their ability to exploit his slow delivery\u2014combined with high-leverage spots in the top two spots of the order\u2014provides a significant boost to our category targets.\n\nOur most difficult lineup decision involved balancing the scarcity of stolen bases against high-difficulty matchups. **Jackson Merrill** (55.37) edged out **Henry Bolte** (40.25) for the final outfield slot, as **Jackson Merrill**\u2019s 13% platoon boost against Cole outweighs the marginal volume benefit of **Henry Bolte**\u2019s leadoff spot. **Henry Bolte** is currently hampered by a poor BvP history and a difficult matchup against Woo, keeping him near the bottom of our \"marginal\" tier. Meanwhile, we remain thin at the middle-infield spot, where **Nasim Nunez** (53.34) is locked in; while his projected #9 spot is a drag on his run production, his elite sprint speed and the opponent's slow delivery offer a high-reward profile for our SB-starved category goals.\n\nInvestors should proceed with caution regarding our top-tier talent facing elite arms. **Wade Meckler** (40.30) faces Skenes, an elite pitcher who drastically depresses his raw projection. Similarly, **Gunnar Henderson** (52.80) faces a challenging lefty in Tolle, with his score further mitigated by a 50% SB-prevention factor from the opposing pitcher. We continue to monitor the IL situation closely, as the absence of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jacob Wilson** limits our ability to rotate for better platoon matches. If **Nasim Nunez**\u2019s batting order is confirmed lower than the 9th spot, we may see his efficiency score dip further, though his defensive utility remains necessary for the rotation.",
